PUBLIC RESPONSE: Filter out genes with log2FC > 2 (or >3 for stricter) in CAR-only vs CAR+IL15 results tables, as these are the most likely cancer contaminants (highly expressed only in the contaminated arm). This can be done post-DESeq2/edgeR via a simple command-line filter such as `awk '($3 < 2) || ($1 ~ /^gene_id/)' results.tsv > filtered_results.tsv` (adjusting column index for log2FoldChange). This is a pragmatic but imperfect heuristic that removes obvious artifacts while accepting some risk of also discarding true biological differences.

(The underlying assumption that IL15 samples are uncontaminated must still be validated by other QC metrics such as cancer-cell marker gene panels or flow data.)

}

